      "title": "Start with the claim and the available choices",
      "narration": "Elena is entitled to a payable life insurance benefit. A lump sum gives her the benefit in one payment. Other settlement options may spread proceeds over time, when the contract makes them available and any binding owner instructions permit the choice. A settlement payment option is different from selling a policy to an investor during the insured's lifetime. Maryland requires a policy offering installments or an annuity to state that feature and include determinable payment information. Begin with the actual contract, eligible payee and payment instructions. A textbook list of options does not mean every carrier offers every option on every policy.",
